## Master Comparison: Square Radiant vs All Square Diamond Shapes

The most requested table in square diamond buying. All specs at VS2/G-H for natural stones, F-VVS1 for lab-grown.

| Factor | Square Radiant | Princess Cut | Square Cushion | Asscher Cut |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Facets** | 70 | 50–58 | 56–64 | 72 |
| **Cut style** | Brilliant | Brilliant | Brilliant | Step-cut |
| **Corner type** | Clipped (safe) | Sharp (chip risk) | Rounded (very safe) | Clipped (safe) |
| **Chip risk** | Low | High | None | Low |
| **Clarity floor** | VS2 | VS2 | VS2 | VS1 |
| **Color floor (natural)** | H | H | H | G |
| **Inclusion hiding** | Excellent | Good | Good | Poor |
| **Fire / scintillation** | Maximum | High | Moderate | Low |
| **GIA cut grade issued?** | No | Yes (for princess) | No | No |
| **Price vs round (same specs)** | −15 to −25% | −20 to −30% | −10 to −20% | −10 to −20% |
| **Best setting style** | 4-prong square | Square prong or bezel | Square prong or halo | Square 4-prong |

**The verdict:** Square radiant beats princess on facets, inclusion hiding, and corner safety. It beats square cushion on fire and scintillation. It beats Asscher cut on clarity budget and light return. The only shape that rivals it on facets is the Asscher at 72 — but Asscher is step-cut and requires VS1 clarity.

