## Square Radiant vs Square Cushion Cut

The square cushion cut is the softer alternative. Same compact silhouette, different edges and faceting.

**Edges.** Square cushion cuts have rounded, pillow-like edges — soft and romantic. Square radiant cuts have straight edges with clipped corners — geometric and modern. This is the fundamental aesthetic choice.

**Fire.** Square radiant cuts have 70 facets producing maximum scintillation. Square cushion cuts have 56–64 facets producing a softer, more diffused sparkle pattern. The radiant's sparkle is more aggressive — more individual flashes. The cushion's sparkle is warmer and more blended.

**Setting compatibility.** Square cushion cuts work well in both square prong settings and rounded halo settings because the soft corners accommodate both geometries. Square radiant cuts work best in square prong settings where the clipped corners are properly supported.

**Price.** Square cushion and square radiant cuts are roughly similar in price at equivalent specs. The cushion is sometimes slightly cheaper because it's more common.

See also: **[Cushion Cut vs Radiant Cut Diamond](/cushion-cut-vs-radiant-cut-diamond)**

